  title: "Operator precedence",
  summary: "The complete built-in precedence table fixes parsing, associativity, short-circuiting, and operator-value boundaries.",
  formsTitle: "Precedence from access through Signal update",
  formsBody: "From strongest to weakest: field/method/index access; application; prefix !, unary -, and Signal read *; **; multiplicative operators; additive operators and list cons; comparisons; &&; ||; Maybe fallback ??; >>=, <$>, <*>, and |>; $; then Signal update :=.",
  typingBody: "Arithmetic, comparison, cons, and typeclass-backed binary operators may be parenthesized as curried function values. Expected types and trait constraints must select one overload. Short-circuit, pipeline, $, Signal, and prefix operators cannot become function values.",
